The final, open age group assumes constant rates.

If \code{infant}, \code{child}, or \code{closed} is \code{NULL} (the default),
then \code{delete_decrements()} checks whether the input life
table is consistent with the \code{"constant"} method or the
\code{"linear"} method in that age band, for all population groups
and draws, and if so, uses that method. Otherwise it uses
the formula from Preston et al (2001).
A life table produced by \code{lifetab_decrement()} with its
default methods is recognized as \code{"constant"}.
